WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.387
Unit 1 is the guide's Step 7.

2
00:00:02.387 --> 00:00:05.447
Create each private link
zone once, centrally,

3
00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:09.151
in the connectivity subscription,
and link it to the hub.

4
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:13.863
The example is Key Vault's zone, from
Learn's Private Link integration page.

5
00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:18.225
Then create the private endpoint,
with a private D N S zone group.

6
00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:23.125
Learn's D N S integration page says the
zone group registers the A record with the

7
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:27.950
endpoint and removes it when the endpoint
goes, so nobody edits records by hand.

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.312
Once the private path works,
turn public access off;

9
00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:35.075
for Key Vault, the firewall's
default action becomes deny.

10
00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:38.392
On premises, add conditional
forwarders for the

11
00:00:38.392 --> 00:00:41.875
vault's public zones to
Azure D N S Private Resolver.

12
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:46.909
And one exfiltration note: a private
endpoint reaches only its own resource,

13
00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:49.625
but traffic to it can bypass the firewall.

14
00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:53.399
Where inspection is required,
Learn's troubleshooting page shows a

15
00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.430
slash thirty-two route for the
endpoint's address through the firewall.
